// Camera stacking setup in URP:
//
// Base Camera (main game view):
//   Camera component → Render Type: Base
//   Culling Mask: Everything except 'Weapons' layer
//   Post-processing: enabled
//
// Overlay Camera (weapon view):
//   Camera component → Render Type: Overlay
//   Culling Mask: Only 'Weapons' layer
//   Clear Flags: Don't Clear (keeps base camera output)
//   Near Clip Plane: 0.01 (very close for weapon model)
//   Far Clip Plane: 1.0 (only renders weapon)
//   Post-processing: disabled (use base camera's)
//
// On Base Camera → Stack section:
//   Add Overlay Camera to the list
//
// Result: Base camera renders world. Overlay camera renders
// weapon on top. Weapon never clips through walls because
// it has its own near/far planes and doesn't render the world.
//
// Performance note: Each camera in the stack is a full render.
// Keep overlay cameras simple — avoid shadows, post-processing,
// and complex culling on overlay cameras.
